 ### Fixed

+- `OrchestratorHooks.onError` now fires for every rejection inside a turn, not only rejections that satisfy `instanceof Error`. When a provider or hook rejects with a string, plain object, `undefined`, or other non-`Error` value, the engine wraps it in an `Error` carrying a readable `message` and the original value as `error.cause`; rejections that are already an `Error` still reach `onError` as the same instance, and the value re-thrown to the caller is unchanged. **Migration note**: `onError` keeps its `(session: ChatSession, error: Error) => Promise<void>` signature, so existing hooks continue to type-check without changes, and `onError` will now also be called on non-`Error` rejections that previously bypassed it (inspect `error.cause` if you need the raw thrown value).
 - `onError` and `afterSession` hooks now fire when `beforeSession` throws, matching the guarantee the hook names imply. Previously, a throw from `beforeSession` escaped the `try`/`finally` block entirely, so neither hook ran. **Migration note**: if your `afterSession` hook assumed it would only be called after a full session turn, it will now also be called when `beforeSession` itself fails — the hook can inspect the session to detect this case (no entries beyond the initial user message will have been processed).

